The locale data of package intl (intl/cldr.bin, which programs that use the
package embed, and intl/testdata/chromium/icu.json.gz and the values in
intl/internal/gen/overrides.go, which it is generated with) comes from:

  - Unicode CLDR 48.2, as cldr-json 48.2.3 publishes it
    (https://github.com/unicode-org/cldr-json), under the first notice below.

  - The ICU 78.2 data Chromium 156.0.8078.4 ships, from Chromium's copy of
    ICU (https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/deps/icu, commit
    5aa526207171ecadf31597f0980a7b7ad8872f33), under the second notice
    below. That copy includes changes The Chromium Authors made to the data,
    such as the Korean names of the North American time zones, which are
    also under the third notice below.

A program that embeds the data distributes it, and has to include these
notices in its documentation or with its copies.

